; Local refinement of the ledger CDDL (alonzo, babbage, conway).
; The upstream rule is `bounded_bytes = bytes .size (0 .. 64)`, and its own comment says: "The real
; bounded_bytes does not have this limit. It instead has a different limit which cannot be expressed in CDDL."
; On chain, Plutus data byte strings longer than 64 bytes are written as indefinite-length strings of
; chunks of at most 64 bytes, which a CBOR reader that joins chunks (ours) sees as one long string.
bounded_bytes = bytes
